      {
        "id": 182681,
        "name": "darkroydante",
        "username": "darkroydante",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/darkroydante/{size}/2044_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-09-23T09:24:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I have no idea if this has been pointed out before, so apoligies for redundancies. My strategy that eventually worked was to lock the Chairman and Rook City's decks. It's not as reliable as Dual Crowbar/Friendly Fire, but I was too impatient to reset until I got that hand, so this happened accidently.&nbsp;Basically, this is more something to just keep in mind as a longshot possibility.</p>\n<p>Incap DW Mr. Fixer&nbsp;puts an envrionment card from trash on bottom of deck. Incap DW&nbsp;Nightmist puts the top card of a trash on top of it's deck.</p>\n<p>It's possible, however unlikely it sounds, to engineer a case where&nbsp;the environment deck is near empty and The Chairman plays Perfect Human Specimines. As long as those envrionment cards aren't Scum and Villiany, and you deal with the Chairman's damaging targets, you can force a hard lock. Nightmist puts the PHS back on top of Chairman's deck every turn, and Fixer&nbsp;alternates&nbsp;Tony and Tremada on the&nbsp;bottom of the envrionment deck, since they will keep getting destroyed by the Villain Character cards.</p>\n<p>From here,&nbsp;Setback can generate tokens and heal himself back to safety, and Expat can just play every single card ever. Then, whenever you want, build up setback's token pool and one-shot the&nbsp;operative and chairman.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>This&nbsp;all sounds pie in the sky rediculous, but I've made it work 3 times- my&nbsp;Steam, my brother's Steam,&nbsp;and my phone, out of proably&nbsp;10&nbsp; or 11 total games attempted. It's tedious, but safe, and you get a feel pretty quick if this setup is going to be possible. (Early prison breaks and scum/villany are your friends.) &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 125,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:07:44.586Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
